# TODO - Native PCI

## Objective

Complete source for exact-device identification, PCI ownership and power D0,
BAR/MMIO access, concurrency, command rollback and safe teardown, based on
documented APIs and public source. **No physical PCI reads.**

## Acceptance

- [ ] Implement/review the stated source and integrate on main.
- [ ] Define exclusive PCI ownership, D0, BAR/MMIO and rollback in source.
- [ ] Ground decisions in public code, published standards and SDK/KDK references.
- [ ] Record unresolved assumptions and fail-closed behavior.
- [ ] Complete with source/static evidence, NEVER requiring a physical Dell test.

## Required source deliverables

- [ ] Implement the controller that retains/opens the actual PCI provider,
      verifies physical 168c:0036 without a 0030 spoof, and supplies genuine
      serialized D0/ownership epochs; wire it into start/stop and power events.
- [ ] Map the provider's assigned BAR with checked bounds, ordered LE MMIO
      and device posted-write completion. Use command-width-safe writes;
      never size a live BAR or invent a mapping/ownership success.
- [ ] Implement sleep, provider termination, partial-start failure and resume:
      revoke callbacks before unmapping/closing, track command rollback and
      refuse access after owner/power loss. State which context may block.
- [ ] Connect read-only inspection and active register capabilities to their
      real callers while preserving TX/DMA/interrupt safety gates. A backend
      contract or permanently disabled source branch is not this integration.

## Evidence

- Source commits, reference URLs/version/rights, static review and lint diagnostics.
- Theoretical completeness only; no build, device scan, packet logs or hardware claims.
